Default $KB_TOKENS_DIR for the compose stack, mounted read-only at /etc/kb in
`kb-mcp`. Empty on purpose: a deployment points KB_TOKENS_DIR at wherever its
real tokens.json lives, and until it does, `kb serve` refuses to start and says
to run `kb token issue`. This directory exists so the mount itself always
succeeds -- see the comment on the mount in ../docker-compose.yml.

Do not commit a tokens.json here. ../../.gitignore ignores it.
